  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "The set of even integers can be denoted by $2\\mathbb Z$. Consider the function $f:\\mathbb Z\\to2\\mathbb Z$, $f(n)=2n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $f$ is injective.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(n)=f(m)$ gives $2n=2m$, so $n=m$. Thus $f$ is injective.",
          "worked": "Let $n,m\\in\\mathbb Z$ and suppose $f(n)=f(m)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2n&=2m\\\\n&=m\\end{align*}$$\nEqual outputs therefore have equal inputs, so $f$ is injective.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $f$ is surjective.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Every $y\\in2\\mathbb Z$ has the form $y=2k$ for some $k\\in\\mathbb Z$, and $f(k)=y$. Thus $f$ is surjective.",
          "worked": "Let $y\\in2\\mathbb Z$. Then $y=2k$ for some $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n$$\\begin{align*}f(k)&=2k\\\\f(k)&=y\\end{align*}$$\nEvery element of the codomain has a preimage in $\\mathbb Z$, so $f$ is surjective.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Confirm that $\\mathbb Z$ and $2\\mathbb Z$ have the same cardinality.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$|\\mathbb Z|=|2\\mathbb Z|$, since $f$ is a bijection.",
          "worked": "Parts (a) and (b) show that $f:\\mathbb Z\\to2\\mathbb Z$ is both injective and surjective. Hence $f$ is a bijection, so\n$$|\\mathbb Z|=|2\\mathbb Z|.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
    ]
  },
